  "result": "The rule and witnesses for `NRS_484B_560_7a` are written, and the gate returned **OK** on its first run (5 witnesses, no composed rules). That used one of the six runs.\n\n**The rule:**\n- **Who it applies to:** a vehicle, written as `ru_aggregate` with the aggregate id `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **When it applies:** there is a railway crossing `c` where two things are true now:\n  - the distance from the subject's body to `c` is under 15 ft (`Units.feet 15`, the law's own figure);\n  - that distance has stayed under 15 ft at every observation since one where the subject occupied `c`, written as `since (dist < 15 ft) (rel_occupies subject c)`.\n- **What it requires:** the subject is not halted, i.e. `drv_motion_complete_halt` does not hold, using the tolerance `p.halt_speed_tolerance`. The obligation names no region, so it doesn't need to pick out the crossing again.\n\n**The witnesses:** the road runs east, the crossing is the rectangle x ∈ [0, 10] m, and each trace has three instants 1 s apart.\n\n| Scenario | What happens | Expected |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | A truck crosses and stops 2 m past the crossing | violated |\n| permit | A car crosses at speed and stops 8 m past | compliant |\n| idle | A car stops at an intersection far from the crossing | not applicable |\n| blind | A car on the crossing with no speed recorded | unknown |\n| branch_1 | A car stops while still on the crossing | violated |\n\nI made no choices beyond the node's own narrowings, so `narrowings` is empty. \"Below 15 ft\" is a strict `<`, as the node words it. I found nothing wrong with the node, so there is no defect report.\n\nFiles are in the working directory:\n- `library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_560_7a.lean`\n- `library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_560_7a.lean`\n- `task_result.md`",
